[{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342104862,"data":"# Kaggle kernel agent guide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342160794,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342165654,"data":"This file travels inside every kernel that `scripts/kaggle_run.py` pushes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342168556,"data":"and is printed at the top of its log. The repository's root AGENTS.md owns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342171288,"data":"every rule; this guide states what a Kaggle kernel is for, what it runs on,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342174102,"data":"and what it must prove before its output counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342177229,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.34217974,"data":"## What runs where\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342182369,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342185335,"data":"| Substrate | Runs | Never runs |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342187962,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342190732,"data":"| Kaggle CPU kernel (the default) | every simulation of 14 qubits or fewer whose widest density matrix stays below `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS`, and the CI gate shards (`kaggle_run.py shards`) | IBM jobs; anything needing an IBM credential |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342197322,"data":"| Kaggle GPU kernel (Aer on GPU, `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4`) | simulations whose widest density matrix reaches `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS` | IBM jobs; narrow replays the CPU runs faster |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342200303,"data":"| Kaggle CPU in the same kernel | transpilation, package builds, the hypercomplex table extraction | |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342203138,"data":"| Kaggle TPU (`TpuV5E8`, `TpuV6E8`) | JAX code only; Aer has no TPU backend. Batch pushes requesting either ID ran on 4-core CPU machines without libtpu, so this account reaches no TPU through the CLI | Qiskit or Aer |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342206134,"data":"| Kaggle Gemma models (attached through `model_sources`) | text tasks on request | evidence: a language-model answer supports no physical or mathematical claim |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342209064,"data":"| IBM Heron (ibm_fez, ibm_kingston, ibm_marrakesh) | 15 or more qubits, or a question about a named device qubit, only after the owner approves a written case | simulations |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342211972,"data":"| GitHub Actions CPU | the CPU replay gate that re-derives a reduced case of each Kaggle result | GPU work |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.34221476,"data":"| Build host (Arch, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB; guide in the untracked `docs/local/`) | development, dry runs, calibration exports, CPU replays, the Arch-packaged hypercomplex stack and SageMath | runs the routing rule sends to Kaggle |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342218108,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342220765,"data":"## Every kernel's phases\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.34222335,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342226047,"data":"`kaggle_kernel/kernel_main.py` writes one JSON file per phase into\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342228854,"data":"`/kaggle/working/output`:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342231452,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342233986,"data":"1. `environment.json`: Python and package versions, CPU model and cores,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342238098,"data":"   RAM, working disk, every GPU (name, memory, driver, compute capability),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342240926,"data":"   CUDA driver version, TPU devices, Aer devices and attached models.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342248602,"data":"2. `hypercomplex.json`: the hypercomplex stack. The kernel fetches the eight\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342251698,"data":"   pinned archives (sha256-checked), installs them through the PKGBUILD\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342254449,"data":"   recipes in `scripts/algebra_package_tables.py`, runs `--extract`, and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342257154,"data":"   stops with exit code 3 unless the regenerated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342259833,"data":"   `docs/evidence/algebra_packages/tables.json` equals the retained bytes.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342262537,"data":"   The build host passes the same test against its Arch packages, so a run\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342265198,"data":"   that reaches its entry used the same algebra code as the host.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342267946,"data":"3. `capacity.json` (smoke kernels): the widest GHZ circuit each Aer method\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342309174,"data":"   runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342318412,"data":"4. The entry's stdout, stderr, exit code and changed files.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342322877,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342326709,"data":"## Package stack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342330687,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342334351,"data":"| Package | Pin | Kernel source |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342338192,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342342081,"data":"| qiskit | 2.5.2 | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342345975,"data":"| qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 | 0.17.2 (the CUDA 12 `qiskit-aer-gpu` stops at 0.15.1 and has no Python 3.13 wheel) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342350212,"data":"| qiskit-ibm-runtime | 0.50.0 (fake backends such as FakeFez; no account or credential) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342354392,"data":"| hypercomplex, hypercomplex-engine, hypercomplex-algebra, Cayley-Calculator, octonion, mathdunders | 0.3.4, 0.5.0, 0.2.0.2, 1.3.1, 0.1.0, 0.4.2 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342360942,"data":"| cayley-dickson, SplitOct | commits abf96e7, e29e72f | GitHub archive, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342369329,"data":"| numpy-quaternion | 2024.0.13 | PyPI (Cayley-Calculator runtime) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342372432,"data":"| numpy, scipy, sympy, pandas, torch | Kaggle image versions, recorded per run | Kaggle image |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342375195,"data":"| SageMath | 10.10 | build host only; a computation that needs Sage stays there |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342377893,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342380485,"data":"## Rules\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342383054,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342385646,"data":"- A kernel is private, has internet enabled (and a GPU when one is\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342388312,"data":"  requested), and holds no IBM credential. Noise comes from a retained\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342391091,"data":"  `gororoba_quantum/calibration_snapshot.py` export.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342393812,"data":"- The entry reads `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE`, which the kernel sets to its\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.3423965,"data":"  machine's device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342399242,"data":"- An output is a numerical simulation. It enters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342402103,"data":"  `docs/state/research_state.json` only after a CPU replay gate re-derives\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342408476,"data":"  a reduced case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342411876,"data":"- The push selects hardware with `--accelerator`; `environment.json`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342414657,"data":"  records what actually ran.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342417452,"data":"- Measured limits of each machine shape, the qubit size guide and the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342420153,"data":"  captured Kaggle documentation are in `docs/notes/kaggle/`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342422822,"data":"- An entry whose output a CI gate recompiles runs with `push --ci-env`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342425609,"data":"  (CPU machine). The kernel then builds CI's Python 3.14.7 with CI's pins\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342428453,"data":"  through `ci/install_pins.sh` and runs the entry under it, because the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342431214,"data":"  image's Python 3.13 and numpy 2.1.3 change compiled depths and durations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342433966,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342436468,"data":"## Aer on the GPU\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342439109,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342441677,"data":"- **Requesting a GPU.** Push with `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4` and a `--timeout`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342444358,"data":"  sized to the work; kaggle_run.py refuses an accelerator push without one.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342447067,"data":"  The kernel installs qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 0.17.2 and sets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342449748,"data":"  `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE=GPU`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342452377,"data":"- **Using it in an entry.** The entry passes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342454992,"data":"  `calibration_snapshot.aer_device()` to `noise_simulator(snapshot, device,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342457709,"data":"  method=...)`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342460303,"data":"- **Noise model width.** Restricting the snapshot and the circuit to the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342462971,"data":"  active qubits (`snapshot_laws.restrict` and `restrict_circuit`) keeps\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342465783,"data":"  Aer's noise model at the circuit's width on either device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342468445,"data":"- **What the GPU is for.** It pays for density matrices at\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342471127,"data":"  `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS` (11) qubits or more and for wide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342473802,"data":"  statevectors. Small dynamic circuits sample faster on the host CPUs. On\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342476478,"data":"  the 7-qubit N=21 order-finding circuits, statevector trajectories took 2.8\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342479148,"data":"  and 36 ms per shot on the CPU, against 21.7 and 54.6 ms on one T4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342481814,"data":"- **Batched shots.** `noise_simulator(..., batched_shots=True)` enables Aer's\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342484494,"data":"  `batched_shots_gpu`, which aborts on any circuit with control flow\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342487168,"data":"  (`if_else` lowers to `jump`), so only static circuits may batch. Batched\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342489856,"data":"  static runs are unmeasured here.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342492466,"data":"- **Replay.** A GPU's seeded counts differ from the CPU's. Its records are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342497635,"data":"  replayed from their retained counts, never by resampling on CI.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342500572,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342503095,"data":"The measurements are in `docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md`, from\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342505816,"data":"`results/kaggle/2026-10-16T204620Z-gororoba-aer-gpu-probe`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":87.342508493,"data":"\n"}
